<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hugh of Montgomery, 2nd Earl of Shrewsbury</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1098</span> · Also known as Hugh of Montgomery</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hugh of Montgomery was a Norman nobleman, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-de-montgomery">Roger of Montgomery</a>, who became Earl of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shrewsbury">Shrewsbury</a> in 1094. With Hugh, Earl of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chester">Chester</a>, he campaigned in north <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> against Gruffudd ap Cynan. In 1098, during an invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglesey">Anglesey</a>, he was killed by an arrow from the fleet of the Norwegian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnus-barefoot">Magnus Barefoot</a>, who had arrived off the island, and the Normans soon withdrew.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hugh-of-montgomery-2nd-earl-of-shrewsbury.jpg" alt="Hugh of Montgomery, 2nd Earl of Shrewsbury" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: S19991002 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shrop.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
